surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>WHF</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>A global, self-consistent, hierarchical, high-resolution shoreline database.</article-title><source>Journal of Geophysical Research</source><volume>101</volume><fpage>8741</fpage><lpage>8743</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004711-Hill1"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hill</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name></person-group><year>1994</year><article-title>Theory of geolocation by light levels.</article-title><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Le Boeuf</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Laws</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name></person-group><source>Elephant seals Population ecology, behavior, and physiology</source><publisher-loc>Berkeley</publisher-loc><publisher-name>University of California Press</publisher-name><fpage>227</fpage><lpage>236</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004711-Teo1"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Teo</surname><given-names>SLH</given-names></name><name><surname>Boustany</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Blackwell</surname><given-names>SB</given-names></name><name><surname>Walli</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Weng</surname><given-names>KC</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Validation of geolocation estimates based on light level and sea surface temperature from electronic tags.</article-title><source>Marine Ecology Progress Series</source><volume>283</volume><fpage>81</fpage><lpage>98</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004711-Powell1"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Powell</surname><given-names>BS</given-names></name><name><surname>Arango</surname><given-names>HG</given-names></name><name><surname>Moore</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Di Lorenzo</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Milliff</surname><given-names>RF</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2008</year><article-title>4DVAR data assimilation in the Intra-Americas Sea with the Regional Ocean Modeling System (ROMS).</article-title><source>Ocean Modelling</source><volume>23</volume><fpage>130</fpage><lpage>145</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004711-LeBoeuf1"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Le Boeuf</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Crocker</surname><given-names>DE</given-names></name><name><surname>Costa</surname><given-names>DP</given-names></name><name><surname>Blackwell</surname><given-names>SB</given-names></name><name><surname>Webb</surname><given-names>PM</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Foraging ecology of northern elephant seals.</article-title><source>Ecological Monographs</source><volume>70</volume><fpage>353</fpage><lpage>382</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004711-Turchin1"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Turchin</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><year>1998</year><source>Quantitative analysis of movement: measuring and modeling population redistribution in animals and plants</source><publisher-loc>Sunderland, MA</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Sinauer Associates, Inc</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004711-Fauchald1"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fauchald</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Tveraa</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><articl